 to entrench the incumbents who can afford army-sized legal teams. Meanwhile, these highly subsidized AI business models remain deeply unprofitable. Approximately 70 to 80 percent of agentic AI initiatives struggled to scale in 2025, according to \"The Next Phase of AI: Technology, Infrastructure, and Policy in 2025–2026\" (2025). When the speculative capital dries up, the companies holding the physical infrastructure will survive, while the downstream startups will be wiped out. Who pays for the damage when these fragile, debt-fueled systems crash?",
